<body>
    <h1>Access token management</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h2 id=3D"Accesstokenmanagement-Tokenrequestflowdiagram">Token requ=
est flow diagram</h2>
<h2 id=3D"Accesstokenmanagement-">&nbsp;<span class=3D"confluence-embedded-=
file-wrapper"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image" draggable=3D"false" =
src=3D"691dc8315306546db3f8fa352364962063a39043e4ffad92a0523c3de4df1fa0" da=
ta-image-src=3D"/download/attachments/1160030741/ComapssX-OktaLogin.png?ver=
sion=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1647371722817&amp;api=3Dv2" data-unresolved=
-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1185389198" data-linked-res=
ource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-re=
source-default-alias=3D"ComapssX-OktaLogin.png" data-base-url=3D"https://wi=
ki.bnc.ca" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-reso=
urce-container-id=3D"1160030741" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"=
5" tabindex=3D"0" alt=3D"" width=3D"468" height=3D"342"></span></h2>
<p>The above diagram explain the sequence of requests made between the brow=
ser and the IDP(Identity provider) which in our case stands to be Okta. <br=
>
  Each step in the above flow is explained in details below</p>
<ol>
 <li>
  <p>The initial negotiation with Okta to verify the user. This is a <stron=
g>POST </strong>call made with the user credentials to verify is the user p=
rofile is active and allowed to authenticate.</p>
  <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
   <div class=3D"codeHeader panelHeader pdl hide-border-bottom" style=3D"bo=
rder-bottom-width: 1px;">
    <b class=3D"code-title">Authentication</b><span class=3D"collapse-sourc=
e expand-control" style=3D"display:none;"><span class=3D"expand-control-ico=
n icon">&nbsp;</span><span class=3D"expand-control-text">Expand source</spa=
n></span><span class=3D"collapse-spinner-wrapper"></span>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl hide-toolbar">
    <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"b=
rush: bash; gutter: true; first-line: 1; collapse: true">curl --location --=
request POST 'https://auth-pp.nbin.ca/api/v1/authn' \
--header 'Accept: application/json' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
--header 'Cookie: DT=3DDI0OwD7yKePSGGPwlfR7y6eyw; JSESSIONID=3DEF100F3562E1=
78678CF6B4E5F125ACA5; t=3Ddefault' \
--data-raw '{
  "username": "mary.james@getnada.com",
  "password": "Tests999",
  "options": {
    "multiOptionalFactorEnroll": true,
    "warnBeforePasswordExpired": true
  } =20
}'</pre>
   </div>
  </div>
  <p><br><br></p></li>
 <li>On successful authentication, Okta generates a unique <strong>session_=
token</strong> which has a finite lifetime(usually 5 mins) and should be ex=
changed for an authorization code before its expiry. <br>
   The two factor authentication sequence is not shown here, but in the eve=
nt two factor(MFA) authentication has been enabled for the user, an interme=
diate state_token is initially generated by the IDP which then has to be va=
lidated with a two factor code to generate the session_token.<br><br></li>
 <li>
  <p>Once the authentication sequence is complete, the application is then =
expected to request a session to be created in the IDP by exchanging the se=
ssion token for an auth-code by making&nbsp; <strong>GET </strong>request. =
<br>
    This requires the application to send across the session_token along wi=
th the list of scopes(for eg. wealth:access-control:viewer, openid).</p>
  <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
   <div class=3D"codeHeader panelHeader pdl hide-border-bottom" style=3D"bo=
rder-bottom-width: 1px;">
    <b class=3D"code-title">Authorization</b><span class=3D"collapse-source=
 expand-control" style=3D"display:none;"><span class=3D"expand-control-icon=
 icon">&nbsp;</span><span class=3D"expand-control-text">Expand source</span=
></span><span class=3D"collapse-spinner-wrapper"></span>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl hide-toolbar">
    <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"b=
rush: bash; gutter: true; first-line: 1; collapse: true">curl --location --=
request GET 'https://auth-pp.nbin.ca/oauth2/aussg4wyd2HZEBGR30h7/v1/authori=
ze?client_id=3D0oa10rgzq8rL3lCZG0h8&amp;code_challenge_method=3DS256&amp;pr=
ompt=3Dnone&amp;response_type=3Dcode&amp;userId=3Dcxtestuser1.dev@getnada.c=
om&amp;code_challenge=3DSVCnKMuE4CB1wjvDvof9QoFl0muOdJICLtcKJ82-ZWg&amp;non=
ce=3DLn28DrFhgxIZN9tRdIcVc4TiE8SKuwKOgigSqO2zCeNHkuOq3DDjpZ4n9dhvL0x8&amp;r=
edirect_uri=3Dhttp%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A3000%2Flogin%2Fcallback&amp;response=
_mode=3Dokta_post_message&amp;sessionToken=3D201112VO1oFuGTNwoM538-VxNNY5Du=
IAxJGFjGD8DcxocxC8mLhyq4q&amp;state=3Dxw8lJc3F1ErxouEhIXUZtshEwl9go6Hpu86YG=
jsjJi0rrGzOoOoNpwq44tYliCl1&amp;scope=3Dopenid ciam:profiles:read ciam:prof=
iles:write wealth:access-control:viewer' \
--header 'Cookie: DT=3DDI0OwD7yKePSGGPwlfR7y6eyw; JSESSIONID=3D9F7779DDC3B3=
C0ABE767FBB2331BDBC0; sid=3D1024NLs1zr5RES5agDZ3Gje3A; t=3Ddefault'</pre>
   </div>
  </div>
  <p><br><br></p></li>
 <li>&nbsp;On receiving the authorization request with the scopes in tow, t=
he IDP validates the user profile and checks if the requested scopes are al=
lowed. <br>
  <ol>
   <li>If any of the requested scopes are invalid, a <strong>policy evaluat=
ion error</strong> is throws and authorization flow fails.&nbsp;</li>
   <li>On <strong>successful</strong> verification, an authorization code i=
s generated and an user session is created in the IDP which is identified b=
y the unique SID sent back in the response header to be stored as a <em><st=
rong>secure </strong></em>session cookie tied to the IDP's domain which exp=
ires or is removed when the session expires or the browser is closed.<br><b=
r></li>
  </ol></li>
 <li>
  <p>Once the application receives an authorization code, it can then be ex=
changed for an access token, that verifies the user's identity for the ongo=
ing session and all its exchanges with external APIs' modules. Each authori=
zation code is tied to a finite list of scopes that were requested in the i=
nitial request<br>
    For future access token renewals, a direct request can be made to the I=
DP to generate a new authorization code that then get exchanged for the new=
 refreshed access token. <br>
    This is accomplished by the IDP verifying the presence of the unique SI=
D cookie in the incoming request and checking if the session tied to it is =
valid. As long as the session is valid, additional tokens can be requested =
with any valid scopes. <br><em><u><strong>Note : A session token that was g=
enerated in Step#3 is no longer required going forward as long as a valid S=
ID exists in the browser session.</strong></u></em></p>
  <div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
   <div class=3D"codeHeader panelHeader pdl hide-border-bottom" style=3D"bo=
rder-bottom-width: 1px;">
    <b class=3D"code-title">Token</b><span class=3D"collapse-source expand-=
control" style=3D"display:none;"><span class=3D"expand-control-icon icon">&=
nbsp;</span><span class=3D"expand-control-text">Expand source</span></span>=
<span class=3D"collapse-spinner-wrapper"></span>
   </div>
   <div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl hide-toolbar">
    <pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"b=
rush: bash; gutter: true; first-line: 1; collapse: true">curl --location --=
request POST 'https://auth-pp.nbin.ca/oauth2/aussg4wyd2HZEBGR30h7/v1/token'=
 \
--header 'Accept: application/json' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded' \
--header 'Cookie: DT=3DDI0OwD7yKePSGGPwlfR7y6eyw; JSESSIONID=3DB4D32E662BEA=
3C7FC840E67DB3862892; sid=3D1024NLs1zr5RES5agDZ3Gje3A; t=3Ddefault' \
--data-urlencode 'grant_type=3Dauthorization_code' \
--data-urlencode 'client_id=3D0oa10rgzq8rL3lCZG0h8' \
--data-urlencode 'redirect_uri=3Dhttp://localhost:3000/login/callback' \
--data-urlencode 'code=3DwQTZKuwvU3aC07-bNiLWYMchZ0iL46OzmPuta1hsUtc' \
--data-urlencode 'code_verifier=3D2938ceeabdb76f88f07e3b9d30ffdbbf963384db4=
ad'</pre>
   </div>
  </div>
  <p><br><br></p></li>
 <li>For modules embedded within the platform, they can now request <u><str=
ong>custom</strong></u> access tokens using the platform session(SID) and r=
eceive a valid access token. By <u><strong>custom</strong></u>, one means t=
o highlight the fact that each embedded application can now independently g=
enerate and use an access token that with a list of their custom scopes emb=
edded that a protected resource can use to validate and enforce access cont=
rol.<br><br></li>
 <li>On receiving the new authorization request, Okta/IDP validates if the =
session user has the scopes requested in the authorization request assigned=
 to then and responds back with either a valid authorization code or a poli=
cy evaluation failure response.<br><br></li>
 <li>If an authorization code is received, it can then be exchanged for a f=
resh access token with the new scopes in them that is unique to the embedde=
d module.&nbsp;</li>
</ol>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
